    "md5": "679c6859d1aab9fb125e1f7c2019f6dd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1206,
    "chunk_text": "To use the service, users must download and register through the \u201cSri Lanka Police\u201d app on the Google Play Store. Once opened, the home screen displays a red SOS button at the bottom centre, along with services including Police News, the Emergency Hotline, Station Finder and E-Services.\n\nDownload and install the \u201cSri Lanka Police\u201d App from the Google Play Store.\n\nOpen the app and go to the Home Screen. You will find the red SOS button at the bottom centre, alongside services such as Police News, Emergency Hotline, Station Finder, and E-Services.\n\nIn an emergency, select the red SOS button when you or someone nearby requires immediate police assistance.\n\nAfter selecting SOS, carefully read the instructions displayed by the app and complete the required steps. If the app requests permissions, such as access to your location, it is advisable to enable them in advance so that the service can function effectively. Location information may be used in accordance with the app\u2019s data-safety information provided on Google Play.\n\nWhile making an SOS request, move away from danger and seek a safe location if possible. In a life-threatening situation, always prioritise your personal safety."
