    "md5": "0602edc3a6d9890e94ceeb9fdf96fa70",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2037,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cFathers should have advised their sons not to steal; what can I do if they are caught?\u201d \u2013 President\n\nPolonnaruwa, Sep 12, (Daily Mirror): President Anura Kumara Dissanayake said claims of political revenge and attempts to gain public sympathy would not deter the Government from taking legal action against those accused of corruption and misappropriation of public funds.\n\nAddressing the \u201cPeople\u2019s Rule \u2013 Two Years Strong \u2013 Progress for All\u201d farmers\u2019 rally in Polonnaruwa, the President said the Government had no personal disputes or desire for revenge against anyone, but had a responsibility to bring to justice those responsible for damaging the country through corruption.\n\n\u201cWhat do they say when corrupt individuals are caught? They claim it is political revenge. Why would we seek revenge? We have no land disputes or personal arguments with anyone. However, we do have a case to settle and that is the case of bringing to justice the corrupt individuals who destroyed this country,\u201d he said.\n\nThe President said attempts by those facing legal action to evoke sympathy by shedding tears would not influence the Government.\n\n\u201cFathers should have told their sons not to steal while the theft was happening. Shedding tears only after they are caught is useless. We will not fall for those tears, nor will we allow sympathy to override the law,\u201d he said.\n\nHe said that the law must apply equally to everyone, regardless of their family background or relationship to those facing allegations.\n\n\u201cThe law applies equally to a grandmother, a mother, a brother, or an uncle. If family members commit theft, they get caught together\u2014what can we do?\u201d the President said.\n\nHe said the Government\u2019s actions were intended to send a clear message that anyone who misappropriates public funds would eventually be held accountable.\n\n\u201cWe are doing this to set an example to the people of our country, proving that anyone who touches even a single cent of public wealth will face punishment one day,\u201d he said."
