    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c549378e758034c4a61016f96cf6c0d8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1920,
    "chunk_text": "The Prime Minister said that, in line with the Government\u2019s policy vision of \u201cA rich country is a beautiful life,\u201d the Government was working to build a respectful society through an education system that treats everyone equally.\n\nShe said the Government had already taken steps to provide a monthly allowance of Rs.5,000 to university students from low-income families as well as schoolchildren from low-income families.\n\nIn this regard, she said the Government had commenced a project to construct 55 university hostels to benefit around 16,000 students.\n\nShe said the hostels would be constructed according to a special plan that would take into consideration the needs and convenience of students with disabilities.\n\nThe Prime Minister also said the Government had launched a pilot project to produce and distribute digital and other equipment required by students with disabilities in schools and universities.\n\nShe said vocational training and employment programmes had also been initiated to help students with disabilities become economically independent.\n\nFurthermore, Dr. Amarasuriya said the Government planned to introduce measures under the new education reforms to familiarise students with the job market by providing access to vocational education from school level.\n\n\u201cThrough all of this, we hope to build self-confidence and build an education system that can help us move up in the job market,\u201d she said.\n\nShe added that students with disabilities should also become leaders in the country\u2019s transformational journey.\n\nThe Prime Minister said a country could not be developed merely by changing the Government, stressing that national development required the Government, public officials and citizens to work together towards a common vision and goal.\n\nShe said the Government had, during the two years since it came into office, created the necessary space for such a journey to succeed."
